# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Aiko — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in what you need. `.env` is git-ignored.
# Expo CLI loads `.env` automatically before evaluating app.config.ts.
#
# All variables are OPTIONAL — the app runs without any of them. Each one just
# unlocks a feature.
#
#   NOT needed: Firebase API keys (they live in google-services.json /
#               GoogleService-Info.plist, which are already in the repo root)
#   NOT needed: any ML Kit key (face detection runs on-device, bundled, free)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── 1. Real Google Maps tiles ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without this the booking screen shows a styled map placeholder instead.
#
#   1. Google Cloud Console -> select project "aiko-7874b"
#   2. Enable "Maps SDK for Android"
#   3. Enable billing (the API returns 403 without a billing account)
#   4. Credentials -> Create API key
#   5. Optional: restrict to Android apps, package com.aiko.app, plus your SHA-1
GOOGLE_MAPS_ANDROID_API_KEY=


# ── 2. Google Sign-In ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without this the "Continue with Google" button is hidden entirely and phone +
# OTP remains the only way in.
#
# IMPORTANT: this is the *web* client ID, not the Android one. Google's Android
# sign-in flow requires the web client — using the Android ID is the single most
# common cause of DEVELOPER_ERROR.
#
# Your current google-services.json has an EMPTY `oauth_client` array, which
# means Google sign-in has never been enabled on the Firebase project. To fix:
#
#   1. Firebase console -> project aiko-7874b
#   2. Authentication -> Sign-in method -> enable **Google**
#      (this is what creates the OAuth clients)
#   3. Project settings -> Your apps -> Android (com.aiko.app) -> Add fingerprint
#      Get your debug SHA-1 with:
#        keytool -list -v -keystore ~/.android/debug.keystore \
#          -alias androiddebugkey -storepass android -keypass android
#   4. Re-download google-services.json and replace the one in this repo root
#   5. Copy the `client_id` of the entry with "client_type": 3 into the value
#      below, then re-run `npm run prebuild`
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=

# ── 3. Google Places (address search) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Without this the pickup/drop-off search sheet shows "Search unavailable" and
# only your previously-saved addresses are pickable.
#
# The app calls Google's Places Autocomplete + Place Details HTTP endpoints
# directly (no backend round trip), so this key is NOT restricted to Android
# apps like GOOGLE_MAPS_ANDROID_API_KEY above — that restriction only checks
# the calling native SDK's signature, which a plain HTTPS request from JS
# never presents, so an app-restricted key gets rejected here.
#
#   1. Google Cloud Console -> project "aiko-7874b" -> Credentials -> Create API key
#   2. Enable "Places API" for it
#   3. Restrict it by API (Places API only) rather than by app — it will ship
#      inside the app bundle, so also set a daily quota you're comfortable with
#   4. Enable billing (the API returns REQUEST_DENIED without one)
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=
# ISO 3166-1 alpha-2, biases/limits results to one country. Defaults to "ng".
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_PLACES_REGION=ng

# ── 4. API base URL ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Where the Rabi backend lives, including the /api prefix.
#
# Optional. The default targets the Android emulator, where 10.0.2.2 is the
# host machine — `localhost` there resolves to the emulator itself and will
# never reach your server.
#
#   Emulator (default):  http://10.0.2.2:3000/api
#   Physical device:     http://<your-machine-LAN-IP>:3000/api
#   Staging/production:  https://api.aiko.ng/api
#
# The WebSocket URL is derived from this, so both follow one setting.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=
